# Audit D5/P3-09: this repo is developed from Windows (git's core.autocrlf
# checks files out as CRLF by default here), but nothing about the actual
# codebase - PHP, TypeScript, PostgreSQL, Docker, all cross-platform - needs
# CRLF. Without this file, every edit made from a Linux/macOS contributor
# (or CI) reintroduces LF and shows as a full-file rewrite in diffs
# regardless of the actual change size - confirmed happening already
# (~25 files with matching insertion/deletion counts, the classic symptom).
# Normalizing here so line endings stop being part of the diff at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.php text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets - never touched by line-ending normalization.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.glb binary
*.fbx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
